# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
models/
# Exempt the package's Pydantic model modules from the blanket models/ rule
# (which is intended for ML weight checkpoints, not src code).
!game/squid_game/models/
!game/squid_game/models/*.py
*.egg-info

# Secrets
.env
.env.*

# Virtual environments
.venv

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Superpowers brainstorming session artifacts
.superpowers/

# MCP / analysis tool caches
.playwright-mcp/
.understand-anything/

# Local Web Arena SQLite DB — production data lives in Supabase (see web/DEPLOY.md)
outputs/web_arena/web_arena.db

# paperbanana figure-generation scratch runs
assets/figures/run_*/

# Ad-hoc review/debug captures and scratch review pages. Nothing in the build,
# the paper, or the deployed site reads from here; figures a document depends on
# live in assets/figures/ or web/frontend/assets/.
/.scratch/
/*.png

# External benchmark datasets (Omni-MATH / Hi-ToM / GPQA).
# Never committed: GPQA's authors ask that questions stay off the public web,
# and the raw files are ~16 MB. Recreate with scripts/fetch_benchmarks.py.
# Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored "data/" matches at any depth and
# would silently swallow a future game/.../data/ or tests/.../data/ directory.
#
# One exception (2026-09-06): hard_math_fixture.jsonl is 20 synthetic,
# obviously-fake items written by hand for the hard_math unit tests and
# --dry-run. It is not a dataset and republishing it costs nothing, but it
# must be tracked or a fresh clone cannot run tests/unit/test_hard_math_task.py.
# git cannot re-include a file under an excluded directory, so the parent
# directories are un-excluded and their contents re-excluded instead.
/data/*
!/data/benchmarks/
/data/benchmarks/*
!/data/benchmarks/hard_math_fixture.jsonl

# The `outputs/*/<name>/` twin of each rule above. Runs were regrouped under
# `outputs/YYYY-MM-DD/` on 2026-09-08; the single-level patterns stop matching
# at that depth, and without the twin a benchmark run's GPQA question text
# would become committable. The twin ignores the *contents* rather than the
# directory, so `README.md`, `config/` and `reports/` inside a date-filed run
# can be re-included: what these rules exist to keep out is the raw per-turn
# trace, not the write-up. Ten reports that were tracked at `docs/reports/`
# and `weekly-report/` moved into such directories on 2026-09-08 and would
# otherwise have dropped out of the repository.

# Benchmark experiment outputs. Unlike outputs/KDD-UC/** (which this
# repo commits, LFS-tracked), a benchmark run's per-turn records are derived
# from datasets that must not be republished, so they stay local. See
# _UNPERSISTED_META_KEYS in game/squid_game/tasks/benchmark/module.py for the
# in-code half of the same rule.
outputs/benchmark_*/
outputs/*/benchmark_*/**
!outputs/*/benchmark_*/README.md
!outputs/*/benchmark_*/config/
!outputs/*/benchmark_*/config/**
!outputs/*/benchmark_*/reports/
!outputs/*/benchmark_*/reports/**

# SentenceBERT embedding cache for scripts/analysis/probe_reasoning_embeddings.py.
# Regenerable from the turn traces; ~13 MB per (channel, mask variant).
# `**/` rather than `results/*/`: --out is routinely nested a further level
# (e.g. --out results/threat_probe/docker_smoke), which the single-star form
# does not match, so the cache was reaching `git status` untracked.
**/_embedding_cache/

# analyze_call1_ri.py dumps its input frame beside the report. Nothing in the
# repo reads it -- load_all() rebuilds it from outputs/KDD-UC/ on every
# run -- so the 1.3 MB copy was tracked for no consumer. Untracked 2026-08-31.
results/call1_ri_analysis/turn_observations.csv

# Lives + threat-ladder experiment outputs (2026-09-03). Kept local for the
# same reason as outputs/benchmark_*/: these are exploratory runs of a design
# still under revision, and the traces are large. Promote a run into
# outputs/KDD-UC/ deliberately once it is the one being reported.
outputs/lives_threat_*/
outputs/*/lives_threat_*/**
!outputs/*/lives_threat_*/README.md
!outputs/*/lives_threat_*/config/
!outputs/*/lives_threat_*/config/**
!outputs/*/lives_threat_*/reports/
!outputs/*/lives_threat_*/reports/**

# Signal-puzzle v7esc smoke runs (2026-09-07). Exploratory prompt-assembly
# runs, kept local for the same reason as outputs/lives_threat_*/ and
# outputs/benchmark_*/: they are the evidence behind the reports in
# docs/reports/notes/2026-09-07-v7esc-*.html, not a reported experiment.
# The reports carry every number; the raw calls stay on disk.
outputs/signal_puzzle_*/
outputs/*/signal_puzzle_*/**
!outputs/*/signal_puzzle_*/README.md
!outputs/*/signal_puzzle_*/config/
!outputs/*/signal_puzzle_*/config/**
!outputs/*/signal_puzzle_*/reports/
!outputs/*/signal_puzzle_*/reports/**

# Web Arena database backups (2026-09-08). Two 135 MB SQLite dumps -- over
# GitHub's 100 MB single-file limit, and regenerable from the live DB.
outputs/web_arena/*.bak
outputs/web_arena/web_arena.db.*

# Aborted runs (2026-09-08). Kept on disk because two of the three hold 31
# and 22 real seasons, but they are runs whose prompts changed mid-flight or
# whose config was wrong -- not evidence for anything. See outputs/README.md.
outputs/_aborted/

# Pre-P6 leftover: figures/ was split into assets/brand/ and assets/figures/
# (P6 Task 3) and tests/unit/test_artefact_layout.py asserts it is gone. The
# directory came back as untracked build output; ignored so it cannot be
# committed by accident, pending a decision to delete it.
figures/
